Noah (docs): Heads-up: we're drafting a soft-sunset announcement for the legacy /v1/invoke. want a tiny, clear migration guide + a short compat snippet. Thinking public notice July 22 with a month-long deprecation window.

Aisha (sdk): I can add a copy-pasteable JS + Python snippet. plan: show old payload -> new /v2/responses payload, mention pinning model@date for determinism.

Ben (infra): we need to document runtime fallback: when model@hash isn't found, requests go to model alias; metric emitted: fallback.model_alias. Prod will also add a throttling rule during the canary.

Noah (docs): good — include a short table: "What changes" (endpoint, model pinning), "What stays" (auth, rate-limits), "Quick checks" (token counts, embed dims).

Aisha (sdk): Draft JS mapping below. Keeping it tiny: preserve user and metadata keys and add a migration header.

Aisha (sdk): ```js
// v1 -> v2 quick map
// v1 body: { model: "rwd-lite", input: "hey", user: "u7" }
const v1 = { model: "rwd-lite", input: "Hello", user: "u7" };
const v2 = {
  model: `${v1.model}@2024-07-01`,
  input: v1.input,
  user: v1.user,
  metadata: v1.metadata || {}
};
client.responses.create(v2, { headers: { 'X-Migrate-From': 'v1' } });
```
Noah (docs): Looks good. Add one sentence: "If you rely on aliasing, expect embedding dims to change when fallback occurs."

Clara (comms): I'll tidy the notice tone. Suggest: "soft deprecation" language + link to enterprise escalation path. Also want a short FAQ line: "Will my Dedicated deployment be migrated?" -> No, managed per-contract.

Aisha (sdk): Python snippet for ops: small curl example too.

Aisha (sdk): ```bash
curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v2/responses -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" -H "X-Migrate-From: v1" -d '{"model":"rwd-lite@2024-07-01","input":"Hello","user":"u7"}'
```

Ben (infra): PR to update runbooks and the Console banner please. I'll set up a canary window: July 18-21 internal, July 22 public. Banner should link to the migration checklist doc.

auto-pr-bot: Draft PR created -> https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5599 (contains snippets, checklist, FAQ).

Noah (docs): Action list: Aisha -> paste final snippets into PR (today), Clara -> review notice copy (tomorrow), Ben -> schedule banner and canary (by July 10), Noah -> finalize checklist and publish notice (by July 15). Thanks everyone. :thumbsup:
